# Build output.
#
# `go build ./cmd/X` drops a binary named X at the repository root, so every
# command gets a line here. Listed explicitly rather than with a wildcard:
# a bare /* rule would also swallow a source directory somebody adds later.
/upicity
/grade
/harness
/bench
/compare
/report
/adversary
/propagation
/drift
/feedback
/explain
/realdata
/validate
/dist
node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
__pycache__/

# Recorded event streams are large (~12 MB of events plus ~3.5 MB of labels
# per 20k-tick seed) and are fully regenerable from the seed — that is the
# point of the determinism gate. `just record` writes them locally for replay;
# the derived artefacts that back the reported numbers ARE committed, via the
# negated patterns below.
results/**/events.jsonl
results/**/labels.jsonl
results/**/world.json
results/**/*.jsonl
!results/**/findings.jsonl.zst
!results/**/metrics.json
!results/**/meta.json
# An entrant's scores are the submission itself, and the leaderboard is the
# result — both are small, and both are what a reader needs to check a
# published number without re-running a model they may not be able to install.
!results/**/scores-*.meta.json
!results/**/leaderboard.json
!results/sweep.json
!results/explanations.json
!results/figures/

# External datasets. Hundreds of MB, not ours to redistribute, and fetched
# rather than generated — so the file itself stays out of the repo and
# data/SOURCES.md records where it came from and its checksum instead.
data/*.csv
data/*.parquet
data/*.zip

# Training recordings for the supervised ceiling. These exist only so the
# ceiling can learn from a run it is not graded on; nothing in them backs a
# published number, and their metrics would sit next to the real results
# looking like results.
results/difficulty-train/
results/train-seed-07/

# Presentation prep — my notes for recording the demo, not part of the project.
# Someone reading this repository wants the code and the numbers, not a script
# telling them where to point their finger.
DEMO.md
SCRIPT.md
NARRATION.md

# Local editor/tooling state, not part of the project
.claude/
.venv-pyod/
